\ Bounded-memory regression for #append's second-operand scratch buffer.
\
\ Each #append used to materialize its second operand onto the context
\ arena, which is never reclaimed on the main task, so this loop grew by
\ roughly 160 bytes per iteration and exhausted the 4 MB cap set in the
\ `.flags` sidecar partway through. The scratch slice now lives on the
\ general allocator and is freed inside the call, so the loop stays flat
\ and prints the marker.

20000 [ { 1 2 3 4 } { 5 6 7 8 } #append drop ] times

"flat" print-line
